- op: discuss  # 8af1
  at: '2026-04-15T20:58:44Z'  # 8af1
  by: agent  # 8af1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8af1
  clock: 2  # 8af1
  nonce: 8af1  # 8af1
  message: "Investigation note: the dead-code-maybe exclusion logic at cli.py:4099-4102 is generic — ANY symbol with non-empty meta.decorators OR meta.annotations OR meta.concepts is excluded under --exclude-annotated. The Java analyzer extracts method-level annotations (java.py:740, _extract_annotations) into meta.decorators correctly. So the residual false positives are NOT from missing exclusion-list entries — they are from cases where:\n\n(1) Spring framework registration is class-level not method-level: `@Controller` on the class doesn't put any annotation on individual handler methods → methods report no annotations → they slip past --exclude-annotated. Fix would propagate enclosing-class annotations to method symbols, or add a separate filter that checks the method's containing class's annotations.\n\n(2) Annotations that appear on parameters (`@ModelAttribute`) — Spring uses these to inject values, but the analyzer extracts annotations from the modifiers node only, not parameter annotations. Spring sees the method as registered; we don't.\n\n(3) `@Bean` factory methods: actually method-level so SHOULD be caught. Worth verifying on spring-petclinic that meta.decorators is populated for these.\n\nSpring is the worst offender; Solidity (using-X-for) and Haskell exports already have separate trackers (WI-jovur, WI-buvun). \n\nRecommend two-step fix: (a) class-level annotation propagation to contained methods (~50 lines in containment linker), (b) extract parameter annotations onto method symbols (analyzer change, larger). Not picking up in current session — this is a focused 1-2 hour task on its own and I want to leave the dev branch at a clean stopping point after 5 merged PRs."  # 8af1
